  "body": "Part of #655. Filed on the maintainer's word (question dialog, 2026-11-12); ours either way: one seam for rows and fields is what lets any look - ours or a kit's - restyle every page at once, and it is where accessible names (see the sibling issue) and units are applied uniformly.\n\nToday `layout/form.rs` and `fields.rs` are the form helpers (about 284 call sites), but many pages still call `ui.button`, `ui.checkbox`, `ui.label` and `ui.add` directly. The estimate on #655 (comment of 2026-11-12) proposes 7 PRs, one per page family.\n\nDone means, per family: no raw `ui.button` / `checkbox` / `label` / `add` left in that family's pages (they go through the form seam, extended where a control has no helper yet); a guard test counts the raw calls per family and fails on a new one; behaviour-neutral (the same commands are queued, the structural tests still find every label); no snapshot PNG touched. Each PR says `Refs` until the last family lands.",
